# .studio-matrix-rules
#
# OmniAI Studio Matrix — Master Orchestration Rules
# Generated: 2026-10-16. Treat this file as the canonical cross-studio contract.
#
# 0. PRINCIPLE
#   All studios (Krea Image Studio, CapCut Video Editor, Suno Music Studio,
#   Freebeat MV Studio, Voice/Dub Lab, Spatial 3D, App & Web Builder, Backend
#   Architect, Cosmic UI Lab, API Connector, Storyboard Supervisor, Recraft
#   Branding, Viral Mockup Simulator, Face-Swap Studio, Vault, Pricing, Admin)
#   are deeply interconnected via the Global Media Link Vault defined in
#   lib/mediaVault.ts (and exposed through lib/studioContext.tsx via useStudio()).
#
# 1. REGISTRATION (mandatory)
#   Any studio that generates an asset (image / audio / video / music-video /
#   beat / pattern / vector / 3D scene / .svg / report) MUST register it with:
#       mediaVault.push({ type, name, url, meta })
#   in real time, immediately after the asset is ready, inside the same promise
#   chain that surfaced it to the user.
#   Local-only copy of the asset in component state is forbidden. The vault is
#   the single source of truth; Studio UI may derive a view via useMediaVault().
#
# 2. CONSUMPTION (manual downloads banned)
#   Studios that reuse assets (App & Web Builder, Cosmic UI Lab, CapCut Video
#   Timeline, Viral Mockup, Voice/Dub Lab, Storyboard Supervisor, Spatial 3D)
#   must read assets from the vault through useMediaVault() and wire drag/drop
#   handlers to accept `application/x-media-asset` payloads emitted by
#   MediaLinkVault, never asking the user to manually download-then-upload.
#
# 3. STATE PROPAGATION
#   Components receive shared state via StudioProvider (lib/studioContext.tsx):
#     - user (id, email, displayName, role)
#     - credits (number | null)
#     - vaultAssets (live Media Link Vault array)
#     - theme (dark/light)
#   A profile edit, theme toggle, or credit consumption event must invoke
#   refreshUser()/refreshCredits()/spendCredits(n) — NEVER mutate a local copy.
#   Components not under StudioProvider fall back to useStudio()'s guest values.
#
# 4. VISUAL LANGUAGE (shared CSS design tokens)
#   Every new studio / panel uses, in order:
#     - `hud-panel` for cards with a 2px multi-color gradient rail
#     - `d3-btn` / `d3-btn--primary` / `d3-tile` for tactile 3D controls
#     - Palette: violet #6c63ff / bright #8b7fff, cyan #00f2fe, green #6ee7b7,
#                magenta #e879f9, red #fb7185, amber #ffb84d, gold #fcd34d
#     - Theme tokens `--hud-*` from globals.css; animated via cubic-bezier curves.
#   Avoid introducing new color literals outside the dashboard palette without
#   design approval.
#
# 5. ASSET METADATA (required)
#   mediaVault.push calls must include at minimum:
#     { type, name, url, meta: { prompt?, resolution?, bpm?, sampleRate?, seed?, duration?, source? } }
#
# 6. STATUS / FEEDBACK
#   When a studio pushes to the vault, emit a short `toast` or vault-count update
#   so the user immediately sees the asset appear in the dock. Otherwise the user
#   will still feel like uploads/downloads are manual.
#
# 7. ACL
#   Admin routes (see /admin) are gated by OMNIAI_OWNER_ID; no other account
#   receives admin rights without explicit owner grant.
#
# 8. BACKEND
#   Missing Supabase edge functions (generate-video, generate-music, etc.) are
#   fine to frontend-stub in DEMO mode. When deployed, hook into the edge function
#   by name (e.g. generate-music-lyrics, save-music-lyrics, generate-image-asset).
#
# 9. SIDEBAR GROUPING
#   Any new studio item must be added under one of three sub-headers in
#   app/Sidebar.tsx:
#     - "Media Creation Suite"
#     - "Coding & Web Development"
#     - "Production & Social Pipelines"
#   System routes (Dashboard, Chat, Pricing, Settings, Admin, Vault dock) grouped
#   under "Workspace" / "System".
#
# 10. PROVIDERS
#   Provider list used across dashboards/assistants must always include Groq
#   (already wired in Supabase provider table) — never drop it.
